,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],"stderr":[],"exit_code":0,"match_count":24,"file_matches":[{"path":"/Users/shreejitverma/.treehouse/SDE-Interview-Prep-3215ec/3/SDE-Interview-Prep/01-CS-Foundations/Operating-Systems/AOS/Part-0-Refresher/R03-Concurrency-and-the-Kernel.md","matches":[{"line_number":22,"content":"## Learning outcomes"},{"line_number":27,"content":"## Motivation and the problem"},{"line_number":32,"content":"## Core concepts"},{"line_number":34,"content":"### Concurrency versus parallelism"},{"line_number":40,"content":"### Process and thread context switch and its costs"},{"line_number":46,"content":"### How the kernel gets control: traps, interrupts, and system calls"},{"line_number":52,"content":"### Kernel stacks"},{"line_number":58,"content":"### Scheduling basics"},{"line_number":64,"content":"### Basic mutual exclusion"},{"line_number":70,"content":"### Function call and return in the machine"},{"line_number":76,"content":"### Process memory layout"},{"line_number":82,"content":"### Pointers, function pointers, and casts"},{"line_number":88,"content":"### Compiling and linking"},{"line_number":94,"content":"### Segfaults and how to debug them"},{"line_number":100,"content":"### Pthreads producer-consumer"},{"line_number":106,"content":"## Mechanisms step by step"},{"line_number":111,"content":"## Worked examples"},{"line_number":116,"content":"## Comparison"},{"line_number":121,"content":"## Paper deep dives"},{"line_number":125,"content":"## Modern descendants"},{"line_number":130,"content":"## Pitfalls and exam traps"},{"line_number":135,"content":"## Practice"},{"line_number":139,"content":"## Lab"},{"line_number":143,"content":"## Further reading"}]}]},"locations":[]}
{"type":"thought","data":"R03 is still a stub."}
{"type":"thought","data":" R01 serves as the style"}
{"type":"thought","data":" model."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nReviewing R01 and "}
{"type":"thought","data":"L04a to align NUMA and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" SMP explanations with"}
{"type":"thought","data":" existing headings. "}
{"type":"thought","data":"Planning aliases for"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the note, including"}
{"type":"thought","data":" SMP versus NUMA, inode,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and block device. Will"}
{"type":"thought","data":" verify URLs before "}
{"type":"thought","data":"writing."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nFrontmatter keys will"}
{"type":"thought","data":" be preserved while "}
{"type":"thought","data":"values are enriched."}
{"type":"thought","data":" Sources will keep the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" official reference "}
{"type":"thought","data":"and add verified URLs."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The draft now includes"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a TL;DR, learning outcomes,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and motivation sections."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The SMP versus NUMA"}
{"type":"thought","data":" section defines symmetric"}
{"type":"thought","data":" multiprocessors as "}
{"type":"thought","data":"systems where all CPUs"}
{"type":"thought","data":" share memory through"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a common interconnect"}
{"type":"thought","data":" with uniform access"}
{"type":"thought","data":" latency."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nCache coherence in"}
{"type":"thought","data":" SMP typically uses "}
{"type":"thought","data":"snooping on a shared"}
{"type":"thought","data":" bus. NUMA partitions"}
{"type":"thought","data":" memory into nodes attached"}
{"type":"thought","data":" to subsets of CPUs,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" making local access"}
{"type":"thought","data":" faster and higher bandwidth"}
{"type":"thought","data":" than remote access."}
{"type":"thought","data":" Modern ccNUMA systems"}
{"type":"thought","data":" remain cache-coherent."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The operating system"}
{"type":"thought","data":" must place threads "}
{"type":"thought","data":"and pages on the same"}
{"type":"thought","data":" node via first-touch,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" NUMA policy, or automatic"}
{"type":"thought","data":" balancing. NUMA multiplies"}
{"type":"thought","data":" memory controllers "}
{"type":"thought","data":"to avoid bandwidth saturation"}
{"type":"thought","data":" on a single controller. Remote latency and "}
{"type":"thought","data":"placement complexity"}
{"type":"thought","data":" are the main costs."}
{"type":"thought","data":" A comparison table "}
{"type":"thought","data":"of SMP versus NUMA is"}
{"type":"thought","data":" being drafted.\n\nAn ASCII diagram of"}
{"type":"thought","data":" SMP versus NUMA is "}
{"type":"thought","data":"being drafted. It shows"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a shared bus for UMA"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and two NUMA nodes "}
{"type":"thought","data":"connected by an interconnect."}
{"type":"thought","data":" Links to L04a headings"}
{"type":"thought","data":" will be included. The"}
{"type":"thought","data":" file system section"}
{"type":"thought","data":" begins with the classic"}
{"type":"thought","data":" Unix superblock, which"}
{"type":"thought","data":" stores metadata such"}
{"type":"thought","data":" as block size and inode"}
{"type":"thought","data":" count."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe inode stores per-file"}
{"type":"thought","data":" metadata including "}
{"type":"thought","data":"mode, ownership, size,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" timestamps, and block"}
{"type":"thought","data":" pointers. The inode"}
{"type":"thought","data":" number is the stable"}
{"type":"thought","data":" identity; the file "}
{"type":"thought","data":"name lives in a directory"}
{"type":"thought","data":" entry. Hard links are"}
{"type":"thought","data":" multiple directory "}
{"type":"thought","data":"entries pointing to "}
{"type":"thought","data":"one inode. A file is"}
{"type":"thought","data":" reclaimed only when"}
{"type":"thought","data":" both its link count"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and open count reach"}
{"type":"thought","data":" zero.\n\nDirectories "}
{"type":"thought","data":"are files containing"}
{"type":"thought","data":" name-inode pairs. Data"}
{"type":"thought","data":" blocks hold file contents."}
{"type":"thought","data":" Indirect blocks provide"}
{"type":"thought","data":" classic Unix triple"}
{"type":"thought","data":" indirect addressing"}
{"type":"thought","data":" for large files. Free"}
{"type":"thought","data":" maps track available"}
{"type":"thought","data":" storage via bitmaps"}
{"type":"thought","data":" or free lists."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nSeparating names from"}
{"type":"thought","data":" inodes allows hard "}
{"type":"thought","data":"links, directory renames,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and open files to outlive"}
{"type":"thought","data":" unlink. Modern file"}
{"type":"thought","data":" systems like ext4 and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" XFS use extents instead"}
{"type":"thought","data":" of block lists, but"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the inode abstraction"}
{"type":"thought","data":" remains. A table of"}
{"type":"thought","data":" structures and an ASCII"}
{"type":"thought","data":" diagram of direct and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" indirect pointers will"}
{"type":"thought","data":" be included. Classic"}
{"type":"thought","data":" UFS inodes contain "}
{"type":"thought","data":"twelve direct pointers"}
{"type":"thought","data":" plus single, double,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and triple indirect"}
{"type":"thought","data":" pointers. Block sizes"}
{"type":"thought","data":" are typically four "}
{"type":"thought","data":"or eight kilobytes, "}
{"type":"thought","data":"with pointer sizes historically"}
{"type":"thought","data":" four bytes and now "}
{"type":"thought","data":"eight."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nWorking through the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" arithmetic for a classic"}
{"type":"thought","data":" UFS inode. Twelve direct"}
{"type":"thought","data":" pointers cover 49152"}
{"type":"thought","data":" bytes. The single indirect"}
{"type":"thought","data":" block covers 4 MiB."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The double indirect"}
{"type":"thought","data":" block covers 4 GiB."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The triple indirect"}
{"type":"thought","data":" block covers roughly"}
{"type":"thought","data":" 4 TiB. The total maximum"}
{"type":"thought","data":" file size is being "}
{"type":"thought","data":"calculated."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe maximum file size"}
{"type":"thought","data":" for a classic UFS inode"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is 4,402,345,721,856"}
{"type":"thought","data":" bytes. A worked example"}
{"type":"thought","data":" will use a 10,000-byte"}
{"type":"thought","data":" file to show three "}
{"type":"thought","data":"direct data blocks and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" zero indirect pointers."}
{"type":"thought","data":" Another example will"}
{"type":"thought","data":" use a 5 MiB file to"}
{"type":"thought","data":" demonstrate exactly"}
{"type":"thought","data":" 1,280 data blocks."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe 5 MiB file example"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is being refined. After"}
{"type":"thought","data":" twelve direct blocks"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and one single-indirect"}
{"type":"thought","data":" block, two hundred "}
{"type":"thought","data":"forty-four data blocks"}
{"type":"thought","data":" remain. These require"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a double-indirect block"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and its child pointer"}
{"type":"thought","data":" block. The total allocation"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is three metadata blocks"}
{"type":"thought","data":" plus 1,280 data blocks."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe 5 MiB example "}
{"type":"thought","data":"is confirmed: 1,280 "}
{"type":"thought","data":"data blocks and three"}
{"type":"thought","data":" indirect metadata blocks."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The triple-indirect"}
{"type":"thought","data":" region requires three"}
{"type":"thought","data":" extra I/Os before the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" data block if nothing"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is cached, which explains"}
{"type":"thought","data":" why modern file systems"}
{"type":"thought","data":" use extents instead"}
{"type":"thought","data":" of block lists. The"}
{"type":"thought","data":" section on block devices"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and the file system"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is next."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nBlock devices present"}
{"type":"thought","data":" storage as a randomly"}
{"type":"thought","data":" addressable array of"}
{"type":"thought","data":" fixed-size blocks, "}
{"type":"thought","data":"historically 512-byte"}
{"type":"thought","data":" sectors but now often"}
{"type":"thought","data":" 512e or 4 KiB native."}
{"type":"thought","data":" Character devices are"}
{"type":"thought","data":" byte streams such as"}
{"type":"thought","data":" terminals, serial ports,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and /dev/null. The "}
{"type":"thought","data":"file system sits on "}
{"type":"thought","data":"top of a block device"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and interprets a range"}
{"type":"thought","data":" of blocks as superblocks,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" inode tables, bitmaps,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and data. The block"}
{"type":"thought","data":" device itself knows"}
{"type":"thought","data":" nothing about files,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and the file system"}
{"type":"thought","data":" issues block I/O without"}
{"type":"thought","data":" knowledge of cylinders."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe write path flows"}
{"type":"thought","data":" from the application"}
{"type":"thought","data":" through the page cache"}
{"type":"thought","data":" to delayed writeback."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The filesystem maps"}
{"type":"thought","data":" logical offsets to "}
{"type":"thought","data":"block numbers via inodes"}
{"type":"thought","data":" or extents, then submits"}
{"type":"thought","data":" I/O through submit_bio."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The block layer handles"}
{"type":"thought","data":" scheduling and merging"}
{"type":"thought","data":" before the device driver"}
{"type":"thought","data":" reaches the disk or"}
{"type":"thought","data":" SSD.\n\nThis split allows"}
{"type":"thought","data":" one block layer to "}
{"type":"thought","data":"serve ext4, XFS, swap,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and raw database files."}
{"type":"thought","data":" Filesystems can reside"}
{"type":"thought","data":" on partitions, LVM "}
{"type":"thought","data":"logical volumes, RAID"}
{"type":"thought","data":" devices, or loop devices"}
{"type":"thought","data":" because all are block"}
{"type":"thought","data":" devices.\n\nModern Linux"}
{"type":"thought","data":" unifies buffer and "}
{"type":"thought","data":"page caches. File data"}
{"type":"thought","data":" lives in the page cache,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" while metadata often"}
{"type":"thought","data":" resides in buffer heads"}
{"type":"thought","data":" attached to pages.\n\nPartition tables are"}
{"type":"thought","data":" merely labels of ranges."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The mkfs command writes"}
{"type":"thought","data":" filesystem structures"}
{"type":"thought","data":" into the block device."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe Linux network "}
{"type":"thought","data":"protocol stack is being"}
{"type":"thought","data":" outlined. The application"}
{"type":"thought","data":" layer uses the BSD "}
{"type":"thought","data":"sockets API and kernel"}
{"type":"thought","data":" objects called sockets."}
{"type":"thought","data":" Ports live in the transport"}
{"type":"thought","data":" demux but are named"}
{"type":"thought","data":" by the application."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The transport layer"}
{"type":"thought","data":" handles TCP, UDP, and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" SCTP. It provides ports,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" reliability, congestion"}
{"type":"thought","data":" control, and checksums."}
{"type":"thought","data":" TCP specifically uses"}
{"type":"thought","data":" sequence numbers, retransmission,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and windowing."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nUDP is connectionless"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and uses optional checksums."}
{"type":"thought","data":" Demultiplexing relies"}
{"type":"thought","data":" on a five-tuple or "}
{"type":"thought","data":"four-tuple.\n\nThe network"}
{"type":"thought","data":" layer handles IPv4 "}
{"type":"thought","data":"and IPv6 routing, fragmentation,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" TTL, forwarding, and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" netfilter hooks.\n\nLink"}
{"type":"thought","data":" resolution maps IP "}
{"type":"thought","data":"to MAC via ARP for IPv4"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and NDP for IPv6.\n\n"}
{"type":"thought","data":"The data link layer "}
{"type":"thought","data":"is device-agnostic. "}
{"type":"thought","data":"It includes traffic "}
{"type":"thought","data":"control, device queues,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" GSO/GRO, and checksum"}
{"type":"thought","data":" offload flags.\n\nDevice"}
{"type":"thought","data":" drivers manage DMA "}
{"type":"thought","data":"rings, interrupts or"}
{"type":"thought","data":" NAPI polling, and the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" MAC address.\n\nLayered"}
{"type":"thought","data":" design allows replacing"}
{"type":"thought","data":" one protocol without"}
{"type":"thought","data":" rewriting the others.\n\nPer-layer headers,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" cache misses, and sk_buff"}
{"type":"thought","data":" copies are the main"}
{"type":"thought","data":" costs of the layered"}
{"type":"thought","data":" stack. Linux packet"}
{"type":"thought","data":" buffers use headroom"}
{"type":"thought","data":" to prepend headers "}
{"type":"thought","data":"by moving the data pointer"}
{"type":"thought","data":" backward rather than"}
{"type":"thought","data":" copying. Sockfs and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" protocol handlers are"}
{"type":"thought","data":" registered via mechanisms"}
{"type":"thought","data":" like inet_add_protocol."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The diagnostic test"}
{"type":"thought","data":" item on ports explains"}
{"type":"thought","data":" that they demultiplex"}
{"type":"thought","data":" many applications on"}
{"type":"thought","data":" one IP address; the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" NIC and IP layer deliver"}
{"type":"thought","data":" packets to the host,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and the transport port"}
{"type":"thought","data":" selects the socket."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe 16-bit port space"}
{"type":"thought","data":" plus the remote tuple"}
{"type":"thought","data":" lets many sockets share"}
{"type":"thought","data":" one address. Without"}
{"type":"thought","data":" ports, a host could"}
{"type":"thought","data":" run only one connection"}
{"type":"thought","data":" per protocol.\n\nThe "}
{"type":"thought","data":"TCP send path is being"}
{"type":"thought","data":" traced. The application"}
{"type":"thought","data":" calls send() with a"}
{"type":"thought","data":" user buffer. The syscall"}
{"type":"thought","data":" trap enters the kernel."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The socket layer copies"}
{"type":"thought","data":" bytes into sk_buff "}
{"type":"thought","data":"fragments or pins pages"}
{"type":"thought","data":" for zero-copy sendfile."}
{"type":"thought","data":" TCP builds segments"}
{"type":"thought","data":" with sequence numbers,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" ACKs, window, options,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and checksums. IP adds"}
{"type":"thought","data":" headers, performs routing,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" sets TTL, and may defer"}
{"type":"thought","data":" fragmentation or GSO"}
{"type":"thought","data":" segmentation."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nNeighbor lookup checks"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the ARP cache for the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" next hop MAC. A miss"}
{"type":"thought","data":" triggers an ARP request"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and queues the packet."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe device layer enqueues"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the packet in a qdisc."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The driver maps pages"}
{"type":"thought","data":" for DMA and posts descriptors"}
{"type":"thought","data":" to the transmit ring."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe NIC reads the "}
{"type":"thought","data":"packet from RAM and "}
{"type":"thought","data":"transmits it on the "}
{"type":"thought","data":"wire.\n\nTX completion"}
{"type":"thought","data":" interrupts or NAPI "}
{"type":"thought","data":"free the sk_buff. TCP"}
{"type":"thought","data":" can release the send"}
{"type":"thought","data":" buffer once the driver"}
{"type":"thought","data":" has copied the bytes."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The data stays in the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" socket buffer until"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the receiver sends "}
{"type":"thought","data":"an ACK."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe receive path is"}
{"type":"thought","data":" being traced. The NIC"}
{"type":"thought","data":" DMA packets into ring"}
{"type":"thought","data":" buffers. The driver"}
{"type":"thought","data":" builds sk_buffs and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" applies GRO. IP input"}
{"type":"thought","data":" routes packets locally"}
{"type":"thought","data":" or to forward. TCP "}
{"type":"thought","data":"input checks sequence"}
{"type":"thought","data":" numbers and fills the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" socket buffer. The "}
{"type":"thought","data":"process wakes up when"}
{"type":"thought","data":" data arrives. recv "}
{"type":"thought","data":"copies bytes back to"}
{"type":"thought","data":" userspace or uses mmap."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nA key distinction "}
{"type":"thought","data":"is noted: traditional"}
{"type":"thought","data":" send performs only "}
{"type":"thought","data":"one CPU copy from user"}
{"type":"thought","data":" to kernel, while the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" actual transfer to "}
{"type":"thought","data":"the wire happens via"}
{"type":"thought","data":" DMA without further"}
{"type":"thought","data":" CPU involvement.\n\nThe send path will"}
{"type":"thought","data":" be illustrated with"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a Mermaid sequence "}
{"type":"thought","data":"diagram and a flowchart."}
{"type":"thought","data":" Two mechanisms are "}
{"type":"thought","data":"being planned: pathname"}
{"type":"thought","data":" resolution to an inode"}
{"type":"thought","data":" via namei, and packet"}
{"type":"thought","data":" transmission through"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the stack. Worked examples"}
{"type":"thought","data":" will include NUMA remote"}
{"type":"thought","data":" penalties, inode block"}
{"type":"thought","data":" arithmetic for the "}
{"type":"thought","data":"5 MiB file, packet header overhead and copies,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and bus transactions."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nNUMA latency math "}
{"type":"thought","data":"is being added to the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" note. Local DRAM access"}
{"type":"thought","data":" takes 80 ns versus "}
{"type":"thought","data":"140 ns for remote memory."}
{"type":"thought","data":" A thread performing"}
{"type":"thought","data":" 10^8 dependent loads"}
{"type":"thought","data":" would spend 8 seconds"}
{"type":"thought","data":" locally but 14 seconds"}
{"type":"thought","data":" remotely, a 6-second"}
{"type":"thought","data":" penalty or 1.75x slowdown."}
{"type":"thought","data":" Bandwidth also degrades"}
{"type":"thought","data":" across the interconnect:"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a 50 GB/s local node"}
{"type":"thought","data":" drops to 20 GB/s when"}
{"type":"thought","data":" reading from another"}
{"type":"thought","data":" node. The note will"}
{"type":"thought","data":" contrast interrupt-driven"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and NAPI polling costs."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nLatency-bound pointer"}
{"type":"thought","data":" chasing and bandwidth-bound"}
{"type":"thought","data":" scans degrade differently"}
{"type":"thought","data":" when memory is misplaced"}
{"type":"thought","data":" across NUMA nodes. "}
{"type":"thought","data":"The note will verify inode arithmetic with"}
{"type":"thought","data":" Python before finalizing."}
{"type":"thought","data":" Ethernet overhead is"}
{"type":"thought","data":" being quantified: a"}
{"type":"thought","data":" 100-byte application"}
{"type":"thought","data":" write with Nagle disabled"}
{"type":"thought","data":" consumes 58 bytes of"}
{"type":"thought","data":" wire time, including"}
{"type":"thought","data":" 40 bytes of TCP/IP "}
{"type":"thought","data":"headers, 14 bytes of"}
{"type":"thought","data":" Ethernet header, and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" 4 bytes of FCS."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nA 100-byte payload"}
{"type":"thought","data":" plus Ethernet headers"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and line overhead yields"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a 178-byte frame. Efficiency"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is roughly 56 percent."}
{"type":"thought","data":" At one gigabit per "}
{"type":"thought","data":"second the frame takes"}
{"type":"thought","data":" about 1.4 microseconds"}
{"type":"thought","data":" to transmit. A ten-gigabit"}
{"type":"thought","data":" NIC can sustain approximately"}
{"type":"thought","data":" 14.9 million packets"}
{"type":"thought","data":" per second at the minimum"}
{"type":"thought","data":" frame size."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nInterrupt overhead"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is being quantified."}
{"type":"thought","data":" At 14.9 million interrupts"}
{"type":"thought","data":" per second, two microseconds"}
{"type":"thought","data":" of processing per interrupt"}
{"type":"thought","data":" consumes roughly thirty"}
{"type":"thought","data":" CPU cores per second."}
{"type":"thought","data":" NAPI polling batches"}
{"type":"thought","data":" sixty-four packets "}
{"type":"thought","data":"per interrupt, dropping"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the rate to about 232,500"}
{"type":"thought","data":" interrupts per second"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and reducing CPU cost"}
{"type":"thought","data":" to approximately 0.47"}
{"type":"thought","data":" core per second. The"}
{"type":"thought","data":" IEEE 802.3 minimum "}
{"type":"thought","data":"frame size is confirmed"}
{"type":"thought","data":" as eighty-four bytes."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nA comparison table"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is being planned to"}
{"type":"thought","data":" contrast SMP, NUMA,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" ccNUMA, and dance-hall"}
{"type":"thought","data":" architectures. It will"}
{"type":"thought","data":" also cover classic "}
{"type":"thought","data":"versus extent inode "}
{"type":"thought","data":"schemes, block versus"}
{"type":"thought","data":" character devices, "}
{"type":"thought","data":"the TCP versus UDP send"}
{"type":"thought","data":" paths, and copy versus"}
{"type":"thought","data":" zero-copy transfers."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nNo required paper "}
{"type":"thought","data":"is assigned for this"}
{"type":"thought","data":" note. Existing L04a,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" L05c, and L07c materials"}
{"type":"thought","data":" will be referenced "}
{"type":"thought","data":"instead to match the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" R01 style.\n\nThe modern"}
{"type":"thought","data":" production server model"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is ccNUMA. It uses "}
{"type":"thought","data":"multi-socket Xeon or"}
{"type":"thought","data":" EPYC processors with"}
{"type":"thought","data":" Linux first-touch and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" AutoNUMA policies."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nCXL.mem expands the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" NUMA distance hierarchy"}
{"type":"thought","data":" by attaching memory"}
{"type":"thought","data":" devices as extra nodes"}
{"type":"thought","data":" or DAX mappings. NVMe"}
{"type":"thought","data":" uses a multi-queue "}
{"type":"thought","data":"block interface via "}
{"type":"thought","data":"blk-mq. io_uring replaces"}
{"type":"thought","data":" traditional syscalls"}
{"type":"thought","data":" with submission and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" completion rings. virtio-blk"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and virtio-net provide"}
{"type":"thought","data":" paravirtualized storage"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and networking. XDP"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and eBPF run programs"}
{"type":"thought","data":" at the driver layer"}
{"type":"thought","data":" before the full stack."}
{"type":"thought","data":" RSS and XPS steer multi-queue"}
{"type":"thought","data":" NIC traffic by flow"}
{"type":"thought","data":" hash. Checksum, TSO,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" GSO, and GRO offload"}
{"type":"thought","data":" further reduce CPU "}
{"type":"thought","data":"overhead. Unikernels"}
{"type":"thought","data":" are briefly noted as"}
{"type":"thought","data":" collapsing the stack"}
{"type":"thought","data":" into the application.\n\nRCU is being highlighted"}
{"type":"thought","data":" as a valid connection"}
{"type":"thought","data":" to this lesson because"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the Linux dentry and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" routing caches are "}
{"type":"thought","data":"protected by it. Distributed"}
{"type":"thought","data":" systems like Raft and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" Dynamo are noted as"}
{"type":"thought","data":" built on local disks"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and NICs, so only a"}
{"type":"thought","data":" brief pointer is needed"}
{"type":"thought","data":" rather than full architectural"}
{"type":"thought","data":" coverage. The Linux"}
{"type":"thought","data":" NUMA memory policy "}
{"type":"thought","data":"list is being expanded"}
{"type":"thought","data":" to include newer options"}
{"type":"thought","data":" such as MPOL_PREFERRED_MANY"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and MPOL_WEIGHTED_INTERLEAVE."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nAutomatic NUMA balancing"}
{"type":"thought","data":" was introduced around"}
{"type":"thought","data":" kernel 3.8–3.13 and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" remains active today."}
{"type":"thought","data":" It migrates pages to"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the local node when"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a remote fault occurs."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nFirst-touch allocation"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is the default policy."}
{"type":"thought","data":" A page is allocated"}
{"type":"thought","data":" on the node of the "}
{"type":"thought","data":"CPU that first faults"}
{"type":"thought","data":" it.\n\nFile system details"}
{"type":"thought","data":" are being added. VFS"}
{"type":"thought","data":" uses inodes, dentries,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" superblocks, and file"}
{"type":"thought","data":" objects. ext4 uses "}
{"type":"thought","data":"extents rather than "}
{"type":"thought","data":"classic indirect trees,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" though it can still"}
{"type":"thought","data":" read ext3 indirect "}
{"type":"thought","data":"inodes. XFS uses extents"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and Btrfs uses B-trees."}
{"type":"thought","data":" Page cache writeback"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is noted. The block"}
{"type":"thought","data":" layer uses bio and "}
{"type":"thought","data":"request structures, "}
{"type":"thought","data":"with blk-mq replacing"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the single-queue elevator"}
{"type":"thought","data":" for modern devices."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe old single-queue"}
{"type":"thought","data":" I/O schedulers were"}
{"type":"thought","data":" CFQ and deadline. Modern"}
{"type":"thought","data":" alternatives include"}
{"type":"thought","data":" mq-deadline, kyber,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" noop, and bfq.\n\nThe"}
{"type":"thought","data":" networking stack will"}
{"type":"thought","data":" cover sk_buff, NAPI,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" qdiscs, and netfilter"}
{"type":"thought","data":" hooks at PREROUTING,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" INPUT, FORWARD, OUTPUT,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and POSTROUTING. XDP"}
{"type":"thought","data":" runs in three modes: native, offload, and generic. Native XDP executes before any sk_buff allocation.\n\nio_uring supports both storage and socket operations. Checksum offload uses CHECKSUM_PARTIAL, CHECKSUM_COMPLETE, and CHECKSUM_UNNECESSARY. UDP GRO is also noted."}
