{"type":"thought","data":"Verified URLs for citations."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nCitation URLs cover"}
{"type":"thought","data":" NUMA memory policies,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" VFS and ext4 filesystems,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" block I/O, and networking"}
{"type":"thought","data":" scaling."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nAdditional citation"}
{"type":"thought","data":" URLs cover network "}
{"type":"thought","data":"checksum and segmentation"}
{"type":"thought","data":" offloads, sockets, "}
{"type":"thought","data":"BPF, XDP, virtio, CXL,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" RCU, and io_uring."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nAdded the mbind man"}
{"type":"thought","data":" page to the citation"}
{"type":"thought","data":" list. The nvmexpress.org"}
{"type":"thought","data":" URL was skipped due"}
{"type":"thought","data":" to a 403 error. Memory"}
{"type":"thought","data":" policy names will be"}
{"type":"thought","data":" limited to the classic"}
{"type":"thought","data":" four and noted as the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" full set is documented"}
{"type":"thought","data":" elsewhere. Automatic"}
{"type":"thought","data":" NUMA balancing via "}
{"type":"thought","data":"the numa_balancing sysctl"}
{"type":"thought","data":" will also be included."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nConfirmed ext4 inode"}
{"type":"thought","data":" size defaults to 256"}
{"type":"thought","data":" bytes. The triple-indirect"}
{"type":"thought","data":" block tree is a classic"}
{"type":"thought","data":" Unix/ext2 model; ext4"}
{"type":"thought","data":" extent trees replace"}
{"type":"thought","data":" it for modern files."}
{"type":"thought","data":" NAPI disables further"}
{"type":"thought","data":" interrupts after polling"}
{"type":"thought","data":" under budget."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nRSS, RPS, RFS, and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" XPS will be described"}
{"type":"thought","data":" at a high level. The"}
{"type":"thought","data":" virtio specification"}
{"type":"thought","data":" covers split and packed"}
{"type":"thought","data":" virtqueues for virtio-net"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and virtio-blk; ring"}
{"type":"thought","data":" sizes will not be invented."}
{"type":"thought","data":" The Linux CXL subsystem"}
{"type":"thought","data":" enumerates type-3 memory"}
{"type":"thought","data":" devices that can be"}
{"type":"thought","data":" onlined as memory or"}
{"type":"thought","data":" used as a NUMA tier."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe CXL claim will"}
{"type":"thought","data":" stay conservative: "}
{"type":"thought","data":"device memory appears"}
{"type":"thought","data":" as a more distant node"}
{"type":"thought","data":" in the same placement"}
{"type":"thought","data":" machinery, so a two-distance"}
{"type":"thought","data":" NUMA model is no longer"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the whole story.\n\nXDP"}
{"type":"thought","data":" hooks run in the driver"}
{"type":"thought","data":" RX path before skb "}
{"type":"thought","data":"allocation in native"}
{"type":"thought","data":" mode. Programs can "}
{"type":"thought","data":"drop, redirect, or pass"}
{"type":"thought","data":" frames. AF_XDP steers"}
{"type":"thought","data":" frames to a user ring,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" while generic XDP runs"}
{"type":"thought","data":" later on skbs and is"}
{"type":"thought","data":" slower.\n\nio_uring uses"}
{"type":"thought","data":" shared submission and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" completion queues between"}
{"type":"thought","data":" user and kernel, set"}
{"type":"thought","data":" up by io_uring_setup."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nio_uring avoids a "}
{"type":"thought","data":"syscall per I/O when"}
{"type":"thought","data":" submissions are batched,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and it supports files"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and many socket operations."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nRCU protects the dentry"}
{"type":"thought","data":" cache and routing table"}
{"type":"thought","data":" lookups so readers "}
{"type":"thought","data":"do not acquire locks."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe bar lists modern"}
{"type":"thought","data":" descendants like qspinlock,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" CFS, seL4, and Raft."}
{"type":"thought","data":" Only RCU, virtio, and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" eBPF/XDP will be included"}
{"type":"thought","data":" in this note."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nUnikernels are a fair"}
{"type":"thought","data":" descendant to mention:"}
{"type":"thought","data":" the application links"}
{"type":"thought","data":" against a library OS"}
{"type":"thought","data":" that still contains"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a tiny TCP stack and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" block driver, so layering"}
{"type":"thought","data":" does not disappear,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" it just leaves the "}
{"type":"thought","data":"shared kernel.\n\nDynamo-style"}
{"type":"thought","data":" stores and Raft sit"}
{"type":"thought","data":" on these disks and "}
{"type":"thought","data":"NICs; the local inode"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and TCP byte stream"}
{"type":"thought","data":" are what they assume."}
{"type":"thought","data":" Link to L09 notes if"}
{"type":"thought","data":" they exist.\n\nEPT/NPT"}
{"type":"thought","data":" maps guest physical"}
{"type":"thought","data":" addresses to host physical"}
{"type":"thought","data":" addresses; a guest "}
{"type":"thought","data":"block I/O still becomes"}
{"type":"thought","data":" a virtio or device-model"}
{"type":"thought","data":" exit. Brief pointer"}
{"type":"thought","data":" to L03.\n\nKSM does not"}
{"type":"thought","data":" belong.\n\nqspinlock will be "}
{"type":"thought","data":"omitted because NUMA-aware"}
{"type":"thought","data":" locking is covered "}
{"type":"thought","data":"in L04b. CFS and EEVDF"}
{"type":"thought","data":" will be mentioned briefly"}
{"type":"thought","data":" since the scheduler"}
{"type":"thought","data":" decides thread placement"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and first-touch, linking"}
{"type":"thought","data":" to L04e. I will check"}
{"type":"thought","data":" L04e, L03c, L07c, and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" L09 only if I need "}
{"type":"thought","data":"to link them. The symmetric"}
{"type":"thought","data":" multiprocessor heading"}
{"type":"thought","data":" in L04a will be cited.\n\nAdditional citation"}
{"type":"thought","data":" URLs are being selected. These cover hardware DSM, L1 and L2 caches, page fault handling, kernel traps, and memory virtualization."}
