{"type":"thought","data":" prereq vocabulary."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nSMP means processors"}
{"type":"thought","data":" share memory symmetrically,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" historically with uniform"}
{"type":"thought","data":" access and no master"}
{"type":"thought","data":" CPU. NUMA means access"}
{"type":"thought","data":" latency depends on "}
{"type":"thought","data":"which memory module "}
{"type":"thought","data":"is used. A critical "}
{"type":"thought","data":"exam trap is the confusion"}
{"type":"thought","data":" that SMP implies one"}
{"type":"thought","data":" bus and NUMA implies"}
{"type":"thought","data":" distributed memory "}
{"type":"thought","data":"without coherence; modern"}
{"type":"thought","data":" machines are both. "}
{"type":"thought","data":"Symmetry refers to the"}
{"type":"thought","data":" OS role of the CPUs,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" not to uniform latency."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nLinux kernel terminology"}
{"type":"thought","data":" uses SMP to mean any"}
{"type":"thought","data":" multicore machine, "}
{"type":"thought","data":"even NUMA systems. The"}
{"type":"thought","data":" course contrast defines"}
{"type":"thought","data":" SMP as a uniform shared-memory"}
{"type":"thought","data":" machine with one interconnect"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and similar latency,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" while NUMA means memory"}
{"type":"thought","data":" is split into nodes"}
{"type":"thought","data":" with different latencies."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nL04a conflates SMP"}
{"type":"thought","data":" and CC-NUMA as alternatives,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" which creates slight"}
{"type":"thought","data":" tension. The refresher"}
{"type":"thought","data":" will follow the course"}
{"type":"thought","data":" contrast: SMP is a "}
{"type":"thought","data":"uniform shared bus or"}
{"type":"thought","data":" switch, while NUMA "}
{"type":"thought","data":"is non-uniform. It will"}
{"type":"thought","data":" warn that modern 2026"}
{"type":"thought","data":" servers are kernel-symmetric"}
{"type":"thought","data":" yet NUMA. ccNUMA hardware"}
{"type":"thought","data":" keeps caches coherent"}
{"type":"thought","data":" across nodes, making"}
{"type":"thought","data":" remote access slower"}
{"type":"thought","data":" but still coherent."}
{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe mechanisms section"}
{"type":"thought","data":" will cover name lookup,"}
{"type":"thought","data":" buffered writes, and"}
{"type":"thought","data":" send path steps. Worked"}
