{"type":"thought","data":"The motivation is that these three topics are the physical constraints under every later paper.\n\nThe note is framed as a story about who pays for remote cache lines, how many copies a byte makes in a distributed service, and how inodes and block allocation shape file systems. The diagnostic test will target SMP versus NUMA, the inode and block device, and the Linux protocol stack. Companion notes on virtual memory, caches, concurrency, and the kernel will be linked to R01 and R03."}
